    {"id":"state-many","type":"text","x":1050,"y":1035,"width":275,"height":75,"text":"Multiple journeys\n2 departures  ›\nChoose by date and time","fontSize":17,"fontFamily":5,"strokeColor":"#174a88"},
    {"id":"rules-head","type":"text","x":40,"y":1190,"width":900,"height":36,"text":"Questions to settle before implementation","fontSize":26,"fontFamily":5,"strokeColor":"#172b4d"},
    {"id":"rules","type":"text","x":40,"y":1245,"width":1800,"height":180,"text":"• A journey is between two specific checkpoint visits, not just city names. Repeated visits remain distinct.\n• Existing departures already have their own checks. Should adding checks here create or link to a departure, including its date and time?\n• Named trip checklists are currently separate. Should a journey use its own checks, or copy a named checklist as a starting point?\n• If checkpoints are reordered or a visit is removed, what should happen to a journey whose endpoints are no longer adjacent?\n• Read-only viewers can inspect checks but cannot edit; family access must not reveal checklist details.","fontSize":18,"fontFamily":5,"strokeColor":"#52647a"},
    {"id":"foot","type":"text","x":40,"y":1460,"width":1600,"height":48,"text":"Illustrative mobile sketches. Desktop uses the same route and status labels with more room for the chosen detail view.\nCounts and status use text as well as color. Long labels wrap; controls need keyboard access and touch-sized targets.","fontSize":16,"fontFamily":5,"strokeColor":"#52647a"},

    {"id":"b2-title","type":"text","x":2300,"y":30,"width":1400,"height":42,"text":"Explore B: journeys in the route","fontSize":32,"fontFamily":5,"strokeColor":"#172b4d"},
    {"id":"b2-intro","type":"text","x":2300,"y":85,"width":1420,"height":55,"text":"Three ways to expand a journey between checkpoints. Each shows the same route, checks and open state at desktop and mobile widths.\nThese are design alternatives, not implemented behavior. The sample journey is Brussels → Ghent, 12 Jun at 09:00.","fontSize":18,"fontFamily":5,"strokeColor":"#52647a"},

    {"id":"b1-heading","type":"text","x":2300,"y":175,"width":1000,"height":36,"text":"B1. Full-width journey row","fontSize":26,"fontFamily":5,"strokeColor":"#172b4d"},
    {"id":"b1-sub","type":"text","x":2300,"y":217,"width":1250,"height":24,"text":"One route, one column. A journey expands between its two checkpoints.","fontSize":17,"fontFamily":5,"strokeColor":"#52647a"},
